# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# ScaleUp AI Simulator -- ignore rules
#
# Verified against what the project actually needs at runtime:
#   * Models/*/models/data/*.json  are REQUIRED model fixtures (extracted paper
#     text and the digitized growth curve) and are deliberately NOT ignored.
#   * scenes/, scripts/, project.godot, icon.svg and the three pyproject.toml
#     files are required and tracked.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# --- Godot 4 ----------------------------------------------------------------
.godot/
/android/
export_presets.cfg
*.translation

# --- Python -----------------------------------------------------------------
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*$py.class
*.egg-info/
.pytest_cache/
.venv/
venv/
env/
build/
dist/

# --- Secrets ----------------------------------------------------------------
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# --- Test and tooling scratch ------------------------------------------------
# conftest pins pytest's basetemp inside the repo so tests never depend on the
# host temp directory being writable.
.artifacts/
.baseline/
.test-tmp/
staging/
staging_backup/
composition/.artifacts/
.mypy_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.coverage
htmlcov/

# --- Editors and OS ----------------------------------------------------------
.vscode/
.idea/
*.swp
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

# --- Generated model output --------------------------------------------------
# Regenerate with:  cd Models/Zielinski && python run_model.py
# Verified NOT to be a test fixture: the Zielinski suite writes its own
# artifacts to a temp directory, and all 223 + 128 tests pass without this
# directory existing.
Models/Zielinski/out/

# --- Ad-hoc runner output ----------------------------------------------------
# A stray result document from a manual run, not part of the project.
composition/out.json

# --- Held-out validation: per-run scratch ------------------------------------
# The graphs and result documents written by
# `python composition/tools/evaluate_heldout_biomass.py`. Regenerable, and ~200 MB,
# because each result carries the solver's full dense trajectory. The result that
# matters -- data/ganjave2022/results/evaluation_results.json -- is tracked, and a
# test fails if the frozen inputs stop matching the digests it records.
data/ganjave2022/results/runs/

# Regenerate with:  cd composition && python -m composition.evidence --result <path>
# The curated catalogue is code, not data; this is only the rendered copy.
composition/evidence_catalogue.json

# Regenerate with:  cd composition && python -m composition.registry --result <path>
# Registry output is generated; the registry itself is built from the models on disk.
composition/model_registry.json

# --- Copyrighted reference papers and figures -------------------------------
# These are publications by other authors. They are NOT distributed with this
# repository. Nothing in the application or the test suites reads them: the
# citation tests verify against models/data/paper_pages.json, which holds the
# extracted page text. All 651 tests pass with every PDF absent.
# `python -m models.source rebuild_paper_pages` is the only thing that needs
# the original PDF, and it is a manual developer utility.
papers/
*.pdf
# Staging deployment candidate (generated)\nstaging/
export/
export_presets.cfg

